        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 88-year-old female patient, admitted on 29/06/2018 due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, clinical examination revealed reduced air entry, prolonged expiration, and accessory muscle use. Oxygen saturation was diminished on pulse oximetry. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory failure. Chest X-ray showed pulmonary hyperinflation without evidence of pneumonia or pneumothorax. Blood tests were unremarkable. The patient was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. She responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. Discharge was arranged on 30/06/2018 with optimised inhaler therapy. Please ensure close outpatient follow-up and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Treating Physician]</div>"
            },
            "code": {
